void on_join(plid pid, unsigned team, unsigned gun, string name) ->
Called when the implementation thinks a client is trying to join from limbo.
Sets relevant state, then calls spawn_player() with the return value of get_spawn_positon() as the position.

void on_switch(plid pid, unsigned team, unsigned gun) ->
Called when the implementation thinks a client is trying to switch team or gun (or both).
Sets the team and gun to switch to when spawn_player() is called.
Calls kill() if the player is alive.
If switching from spectator to non-spectator, LSd calls spawn_player() and immediately kills the player again; other implementations may differ.

void tick(void) ->
Called at a rate of TICKRATE&nbsp;Hz by the event loop (see <a rel=noreferrer href="https://66.135.15.57/lsd/tree/src/main.c#:~:text=static%20void%20do_loop("><code>src/main.c:do_loop()</code></a>).
Handles the following by default:
<ul>
<li>Player physics; tick_player_physics()
<li>Player respawning; spawn_player()
<li>Player gun reloading; reload_player()
<li>Player gunfire estimation (no dedicated function)
<li>Grenade detonation; detonate_grenade() <!-- TODO: better specify that it's server-local! -->
<li>Grenade physics (no dedicated function) <!-- TODO: dedicate function -->
<li>Sending position/orientation to clients; send_player_update()
</ul>

